{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344064-a-requiem-version-of-chimestry","id":1344064,"title":"A Requiem version of Chimestry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-27T14:08:56-07:00","id":1344064,"title":"A Requiem version of Chimestry","content":"Hi, i'm storytelling a campaign of &quot;Masquiem&quot;, so basically Masquerade lore and Requiem rules.<br /> I was trying to convert or create some kind of equivalent for the main 13 clan disciplines, most went without problems ( I was helped a lot by the fact that there is plenty of disciplines in Requiem that you can use as source of inspiration for a good conversion of the old Masquerade's discipline).<br /> But I have quite the trouble creating a reliable version of Chimestry, the illusory power of the Ravnos Clan. <br /> <br /> How would you make it? Or from where should I find inspiration?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T15:00:27-07:00","id":1344077,"title":"","content":"Not being a Masquerade fan I\u2019m thinking about Nightmare and Obfuscate devotions but I\u2019m guessing that\u2019s not what you\u2019re looking for. If you tell me what you\u2019re looking for it to do I might have a better idea of how to make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T16:54:07-07:00","id":1344089,"title":"","content":"I have thought about this subject!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35RmMyVmprSnJ4QVU/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-UdsMclFMZVaBensF6HdBkw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35RmMyVmprSnJ4QVU/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-UdsMclFMZVaBensF6HdBkw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35RmMyVmprSnJ4QVU/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-UdsMclFMZVaBensF6HdBkw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35RmMyVmprSnJ4QVU/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-UdsMclFMZVaBensF6HdBkw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nightmare, Obfuscate, and a slightly rejiggered version of the one in V20 all work. The V20 Chimerstry system follows the Requiem ethos of building on the basic power quite well.<br /> <br /> I'd say Obfuscate is a pretty good choice, though, as it does create illusions at higher levels. Maybe reskin the Obfuscate powers to be more about false images rather than invisibility. Or maybe the Ravnos have the ability to lend their Resilience to certain Obfuscate illusions in order to make them more solid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":".  Fixed the link, which apparently people are still clicking on? 12-18-2021, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T18:39:15-07:00","id":1344107,"title":"","content":"Honestly, why not do it as a group of Obfuscate-Nightmare devotions? It's the &quot;quick, dirty &amp; close enough&quot; adaptation that comes to mind.<br /> <br /> Or if you're up to something wicked, Chimerstry Dominate+Dementation devotions - and the Julii were not Ventrue, but <b><i>Ravnos</i></b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T19:00:50-07:00","id":1344110,"title":"","content":"If you really want to use Masquerade lore, I'd take the V5 approach and try to cut down the number of Disciplines. Does &quot;transform into a snake&quot; really need to be totally separate from &quot;transform into any animal that isn't a snake&quot;?<br /> <br /> Yossarian's homebrew takes this approach, and it seems to fit well. I'd probably go one step farther and merge Vicissitude into Protean; I think that's the only Special Unique Thing left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T00:46:52-07:00","id":1344146,"title":"","content":"The Vampire Translation Guide is always a good source for any porting ideas you may have. It covers both Ravnos and Chimestry pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T01:50:14-07:00","id":1344151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344064-a-requiem-version-of-chimestry#post1344064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, i'm storytelling a campaign of &amp;quot;Masquiem&amp;quot;, so basically Masquerade lore and Requiem rules.<br /> I was trying to convert or create some kind of equivalent for the main 13 clan disciplines, most went without problems ( I was helped a lot by the fact that there is plenty of disciplines in Requiem that you can use as source of inspiration for a good conversion of the old Masquerade's discipline).<br /> But I have quite the trouble creating a reliable version of Chimestry, the illusory power of the Ravnos Clan. <br /> <br /> How would you make it? Or from where should I find inspiration?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Chimestry is about fairy hallucinations, Nightmare is about Nightmarish Hallucinations. I would convert then Chimestry as Devotions combining Nightmare and Majesty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T07:03:53-07:00","id":1345224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344064-a-requiem-version-of-chimestry?p=1344151#post1344151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chimestry is about fairy hallucinations, Nightmare is about Nightmarish Hallucinations. I would convert then Chimestry as Devotions combining Nightmare and Majesty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, Nightmare+[your pick here] should work well enough overall, what one picks, if pure Nightmare or mixing with the mental discipline of mental discipline of one's choice, depending just on what kind of themes and imagery one might wish to explore with illusion/hallucination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T10:33:31-07:00","id":1345264,"title":"","content":"My best recommendation is going to more or less follow the same lines as the other commentators, except:<br /> <br /> Define the bloodline devotions first, then work your way back into the rest of the clan/bloodline writeup.<br /> <br /> Why? Because you want a sensible CofD power portrayal before you end up writing fluff, in-clan disciplines and the like. If the unique clan powerset makes sense the rest will follow.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'd recommend making Chimestry into a set of Devotions. Probably combining some mix of Obfuscate, Nightmare, Auspex and Majesty; I'd have to pour through WoD Chimestry writeups again to say for sure. <br /> <br /> But what I want to remember is that Chimestry only did illusions--they were not real, and any effects generated were psychosomatic in nature. Now: at higher levels, yes, those psychosomatic effects could bloody well kill you dead, and you had virtually no way to dismiss them, but Nightmare works very similarly. <br /> <br /> Consider that VtR powers at 5 are roughly analogous to WoD at 6. You can calibrate accordingly and develop a proper set of devotions from that. Also keep in mind that some Disciplines may cover the functionality you look for already (Nightmare in particular).<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T04:00:31-07:00","id":1345415,"title":"","content":"Surely at this point Nightmare looks like the most promising lead to follow. I will work on that. <br /> I'd like to avoid using Obfuscate because that's a Ravnos' discipline as well, and so it would be some kind of double.<br /> <br /> Do you know of any powers of other gamelines of Chronicles of Darkness that might be worth looking into?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:29:15-08:00","id":1345824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344064-a-requiem-version-of-chimestry?p=1345415#post1345415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely at this point Nightmare looks like the most promising lead to follow. I will work on that.<br /> I'd like to avoid using Obfuscate because that's a Ravnos' discipline as well, and so it would be some kind of double.<br /> <br /> Do you know of any powers of other gamelines of Chronicles of Darkness that might be worth looking into?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you could do Ravnos as a bloodline of some group (Gangrel if you're into metaplot) that has Nightmare and Obfuscate, Fortitude and Animalism. Then, give them access to Bloodline-specific Devotions (i.e. prerequisite &quot;Ravnos Bloodline&quot; for purchase) that members call &quot;Chimestry&quot; and make up the powerset you need to portray their illusion powers.<br /> <br /> Some WoD powers of Chimestry can be handled by straight Nightmare. Some by Obfuscate. Almost all the remainder should be doable through some combination of Nightmare+Obfuscate+Fortitude Devotions, where Fortitude acts to &quot;fortify&quot; the mental illusion effect and give it greater durability in the mind. Or something like that.<br /> <br /> If you cobble together something please share--would be interesting to see.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T19:19:59-08:00","id":1348106,"title":"","content":"I would consider it an isolated variant of Dominate. Is it not imposing a chosen version of reality on a victim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T14:43:36-08:00","id":1348732,"title":"","content":"When our group workshopped this for our Masquiem game (which sadly never really got off the ground), we had the Ravnos as a Daeva bloodline with this Discipline spread: (Majesty, Celerity, Vigor, Nightmare). This would be if you wanted to focus on Rav as charismatic and energetic, using illusions to pass things off as better or worse than they truly are. It's helpful to note how Devotions can sometimes use the physical disciplines metaphorically, such as Resilience allowing an effect to persist or Vigor making it &quot;forceful.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Translation Guide also floats the idea of doing them as a Gangrel bloodline. This would be closer for their traditional Discipline spread (Animalism, Resilience, Protean, Obfuscate). Here I'd run with Chimerstry being Devotions of Protean and Obfuscate, designed to assist the Ravnos as a canny survivor whose illusions draw prey in or alter the playing field.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:51:03-08:00","id":1350059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1344064-a-requiem-version-of-chimestry?p=1348106#post1348106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would consider it an isolated variant of Dominate. Is it not imposing a chosen version of reality on a victim?</div> </div> </div> </div>Naa. It does not fit at all imho. Dominate alters memories. You already can command someone to remember they saw a specific hallucination. Or you can already command them to act as they are seing that hallucination.<br /> Chimestry is another thing, another flavor of Nightmare 4 I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}